{
  "name": "Almost DX7",
  "description": "Dry six-operator FM/PM synthesizer with eight algorithms. Preset is an integer performance controller (1–32). 1: Tine Piano; 2: Soft Electric Piano; 3: FM Bass; 4: Slap Bass; 5: Glass Bell; 6: Wooden Mallet; 7: Synth Brass; 8: Digital Organ; 9: Bright Pluck; 10: Evolving Pad; 11: Metallic Lead; 12: Shimmer Keys; 13: Solid Sub Bass; 14: Rubber Synth Bass; 15: Fingered FM Bass; 16: Picked FM Bass; 17: Fretless FM Bass; 18: Octave Slap Bass; 19: Hollow Square Bass; 20: Growl Bass; 21: FM Clavinet; 22: Metallic Tom; 23: Wire Snare; 24: Space Chime; 25: Crosswind; 26: Whistling Draft; 27: Anvil Strike; 28: Brake Drum; 29: Sheet Metal Crash; 30: Scanner Blip; 31: Reactor Startup; 32: Alien Transmission. Brightness, Attack, Release, Vibrato and Output affect new notes. Per-operator ADSRs and velocity response are inside FM6. Edit FM6 to design a custom voice; select preset 0 there and disconnect the preset controller (or extend its minimum to 0). Centered Stereo Output; add effects in mixer routing. 16 simultaneous voices. Inspired by 1980s FM, without DX7 patch/SysEx compatibility.",
